      "problem": "Which of the following shows the graph of $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,$ and then use the formula $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $3$ | $13$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/b43e0f6b6f359b08dd346a30509d82482a3b82defac90728ddaa7c9769690846.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/8de7d3c268e35f85da8f1bf7882d2ebd285fa3f5c0c239c986eeb1564277e4e1.png)",
